## Original Content
<p>Brazil passed the General Data Protection Law in 2018, and it will come into effect February 2020. This article examines the GDPR vs. the LGPD, how it differs, and...</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://gdpr.eu/gdpr-vs-lgpd/">What is the LGPD? Brazil’s version of the GDPR</a> appeared first on <a href="https://gdpr.eu">GDPR.eu</a>.</p>

## Summary
The article explains that the LGPD is Brazil's version of the GDPR, a data protection law passed in 2018. It will come into effect in February 2020 and the article compares it to the GDPR.

## Key Points
- LGPD is Brazil's General Data Protection Law.
- It is modeled after the EU's GDPR.
- The law was enacted in 2018 and will be effective from February 2020.


